{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/641193-the-lunar-landing-in-wta","id":641193,"title":"The Lunar Landing in WtA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-26T23:25:41-07:00","id":641193,"title":"The Lunar Landing in WtA","content":"Something I just realized is that the moon landing seems to have had very little if any repercussions in the world of WtA. Both CtD and WtF portray the first lunar visit as significant, with one being the beginning of a new age of wonder (or something) and the other being a catastrophe that brought evil spirits back to earth. Apes crawling around on a hitherto pristine Celestine might have some effect... though I am not sure what. Glancing through Raga Across the Heavens didn't turn up much, and the entry on Luna is pretty limited. Am I just missing something or is this just something that isn't addressed in WtA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T00:34:36-07:00","id":641256,"title":"","content":"The hard, lifeless physical shell of Luna matters very little when her true presence and power are in her Umbral guise. Werewolf not being Mage and all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I'm pretty sure the shifters would care if someone decided to colonize her, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T08:14:21-07:00","id":641593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/641193-the-lunar-landing-in-wta#post641193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I just realized is that the moon landing seems to have had very little if any repercussions in the world of WtA. Both CtD and WtF portray the first lunar visit as significant, with one being the beginning of a new age of wonder (or something) and the other being a catastrophe that brought evil spirits back to earth. Apes crawling around on a hitherto pristine Celestine might have some effect... though I am not sure what. Glancing through Raga Across the Heavens didn't turn up much, and the entry on Luna is pretty limited. Am I just missing something or is this just something that isn't addressed in WtA?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing to metaphysically keep in mind is that -- unlike with some Changelings and Mages -- Garou are very Gaia/Middle-Umbra focused; even with their connection to Luna (and a small percentage of them making umbral trips there/beyond), the moon-landing, in-and-of-itself, is just &quot;another sign of the Weaver sending out another thread&quot;. It's important, yes, but cosmologically speaking (from the Garou POV) it's not that big a deal. Way worse shit is happening, and has *been* happening, on Earth/Gaia *right now*. Luna is fine, by comparison. (For Changelings, the landing on the moon, in the physical sense, means almost nothing -- it's the sense of wonder/possibility that exploded across the world when hundreds of millions of humans all &quot;looked up&quot; (symbolically, via their televisions) and *believed*. That made the Arcadian-link via the Moon &quot;open&quot;, and manifested a surge of Glamour, as well. Very important distinction from the Garou, who operate via the Middle-Umbra relative to the Moon, vs. the Changelings/Fae, who interact with it via The Dreaming, which is a step &quot;above&quot; the Middle Umbra, though a step &quot;below&quot; the High Umbra. The metaphysics can get a bit heady, true, but again to restate: the Lunar Landing was a &quot;thing&quot; to the Garou, no question... but it just wasn't that big a deal, as the physical interaction had little to do with *Luna*, as a spirit, so the werewolves just shrugged.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T08:14:38-07:00","id":641595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/641193-the-lunar-landing-in-wta#post641193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I just realized is that the moon landing seems to have had very little if any repercussions in the world of WtA. Both CtD and WtF portray the first lunar visit as significant, with one being the beginning of a new age of wonder (or something) and the other being a catastrophe that brought evil spirits back to earth. Apes crawling around on a hitherto pristine Celestine might have some effect... though I am not sure what. Glancing through Raga Across the Heavens didn't turn up much, and the entry on Luna is pretty limited. Am I just missing something or is this just something that isn't addressed in WtA?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if it's from a book, but one Lunar Myth in my WoD is that She wasn't a hitherto pristine Celestine. She was once vibrant and full of life, but the Wyrm destroyed it all. That is why you refill your Rage when you look upon her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T12:19:06-07:00","id":1486172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/641193-the-lunar-landing-in-wta?p=641595#post641595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure if it's from a book, but one Lunar Myth in my WoD is that She wasn't a hitherto pristine Celestine. She was once vibrant and full of life, but the Wyrm destroyed it all. That is why you refill your Rage when you look upon her.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ananasi mythos have Wyrm and Weaver battling on the surface of the moon, and their fight destroyed all of the satellite's life. The lore presented at the start of that book seems to be pretty accurate and there's no reason to doubt QA's account, though of course Garou wouldn't necessarily know anything more than that the Wyrm was involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T12:24:07-07:00","id":1486358,"title":"","content":"Mage has something weirder. There are/were two separate bases involving the moon. The Society of Ether had a satellite chantry orbiting the moon where forays deeper into the Umbra could start from, Victoria Station. Those on the station never saw anything land on the moon. Neither did the Void Engineers at Darkside Moonbase, albeit they were on the other side of the moon. Various Mage reports include seeing were creatures (Bastet?) and stranger things, possibly fae-related. There's also a Dark Umbra on the moon where ghosts from a explosion at the moon base. Which 'layer' of the Umbra these things are happening are still in question. Most of this comes from <i>\u200bBeyond the Barriers: The Book of Worlds</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T16:50:04-07:00","id":1486374,"title":"","content":"Metaphysically speaking. The actual moon might not be as important as the image of the moon as seen from earth. Out-space isn't really the Garou's thing and it doesn't have much to do with werewolf cosmology in most cases.<br /> <br /> There Are books that have gone into the subject, but I believe the reception for them has been mixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T17:23:28-07:00","id":1486378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/641193-the-lunar-landing-in-wta?p=1486374#post1486374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metaphysically speaking. The actual moon might not be as important as the image of the moon as seen from earth. Out-space isn't really the Garou's thing and it doesn't have much to do with werewolf cosmology in most cases.<br /> <br /> There Are books that have gone into the subject, but I believe the reception for them has been mixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can literally fly through its spiritual reflection (The Aetherial Realm) and have a much easier time getting there, arguably, than NASA does getting up through the physical realm in the same place. It's also full of signs and portents as well as wisdom for the Changers, so I would say that their cosmology has an awful lot to do with it, and it is, in fact, their thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T22:24:15-07:00","id":1486389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/641193-the-lunar-landing-in-wta?p=641595#post641595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure if it's from a book, but one Lunar Myth in my WoD is that She wasn't a hitherto pristine Celestine. She was once vibrant and full of life, but the Wyrm destroyed it all. That is why you refill your Rage when you look upon her.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was the Weaver, her early sign of insanity<br /> She froze everything in perfect stasis, so to speak, made Luna an example what the world, the whole universe - at least in her eyes- should be<br /> The Rokea alreay existed back then (they not really good source of information, to them, the Moon is just the Wound (sun) covered with balm) as well as the Insect Races (exterminated)<br /> And of course the Mokol\u00e9... it was before the Age of Kings, so its debatable any Mokol\u00e9 could remember the time when Earth's companion was vibrant and full of life &quot;mini-earth&quot;<br /> But we don't really have reason to doubt Ananasa's words<br /> I guess the Garou would never swallow the &quot;fact&quot; (lack of better words) they fought the wrong enemy in the past few millenium<br /> The Rokea are suprisingly insightfull in that matter &quot;They wrere created to fight against a big bad evil, but there was none... so they started to fight against everything, including themselves&quot; - not exact words, but you get the picture<br /> Strangely enough, almost everyone belives, Gaia is not the center of everything but &quot;just&quot; the Earth, and Weaver/Wyld/Dragon of Balance are universal entities (In fact, in one of the end of the world scenarios, when Ananasa freed the Wyrm, a good portion of the Universe was destroyed and Weaver came to her senses)<br /> Wich actually make sense and makes the Garou self centered and quite deluded tragic figures<br /> I think they simply can't comprehend, Gaia and by that Them are not the center of the universe. If the Moon was full of life story is not just a story, but a fact and true that basically would shatter their core identiy and would toss the whole race in to eternal Horano<br /> WW20 Black Spiral Dancers basically built around that fact: What war? We are alreay won dude, Enjoy existence while it last, the &quot;Apocalypse&quot; came and you just failed to notice. Gaia will soon die, but thats okay, Spirits reborn, It will be better next time... wan' another beer?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T07:59:42-07:00","id":1486418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/641193-the-lunar-landing-in-wta?p=1486389#post1486389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It was the Weaver, her early sign of insanity<br /> She froze everything in perfect stasis, so to speak, made Luna an example what the world, the whole universe - at least in her eyes- should be<br /> The Rokea alreay existed back then (they not really good source of information, to them, the Moon is just the Wound (sun) covered with balm) as well as the Insect Races (exterminated)<br /> And of course the Mokol\u00e9... it was before the Age of Kings, so its debatable any Mokol\u00e9 could remember the time when Earth's companion was vibrant and full of life &quot;mini-earth&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>None that survived the War of Rage, anyway. Mnesis used to stretch back further, but it got put through the blender by wars with the Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But we don't really have reason to doubt Ananasa's words </div> </div> </div>She's a high-end Triatic manifestation. Even without a reason to lie, her creator could have embedded failsafes and coded obedience into her without her being completely aware of it. The Weaver's fall was far more meticulous and slow than the Unmaker; it would give her plenty of time to start breaking her own toys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess the Garou would never swallow the &quot;fact&quot; (lack of better words) they fought the wrong enemy in the past few millenium </div> </div> </div>Fighting their allies was fighting the wrong enemy. Fighting the manifestations of the Triatic Wyrms was not, by any means, &quot;fighting the wrong enemy&quot;, because left alone, they would have destroyed the Tellurian, and as we can see in Apocalypse, a raid on Malfeas to free the untainted, uncrazed core of the Wyrm is very much the height of &quot;Safety Not Guaranteed&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Rokea are suprisingly insightfull in that matter &quot;They wrere created to fight against a big bad evil, but there was none... so they started to fight against everything, including themselves&quot; - not exact words, but you get the picture<br /> Strangely enough, almost everyone belives, Gaia is not the center of everything but &quot;just&quot; the Earth, and Weaver/Wyld/Dragon of Balance are universal entities (In fact, in one of the end of the world scenarios, when Ananasa freed the Wyrm, a good portion of the Universe was destroyed and Weaver came to her senses) </div> </div> </div>That got chucked out for Revised. Mostly because it was heavily undermining the central premise of the game, i.e., Gaia was the most important thing, that is why you are still fighting. It's comparable to the condensing and elimination of paths from Vampire to make Humanity more important in later-edition V:tM. No more Path of What I Was Going to Do Anyway; you actually have to work to maintain control over yourself. Similarly, the Fera are all pitching in for Gaia, and there's a fairly pristine example of how and why in the Beast Courts. It's also part of the common cause that brings together the Ahadi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wich actually make sense and makes the Garou self centered and quite deluded tragic figures<br /> I think they simply can't comprehend, Gaia and by that Them are not the center of the universe. If the Moon was full of life story is not just a story, but a fact and true that basically would shatter their core identiy and would toss the whole race in to eternal Horano </div> </div> </div>No, in this game, Gaia is of prime importance. Whether one spirit is higher than the other is pretty much immaterial to this premise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WW20 Black Spiral Dancers basically built around that fact </div> </div> </div>What fact?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> : What war? We are alreay won dude, Enjoy existence while it last, the &quot;Apocalypse&quot; came and you just failed to notice. Gaia will soon die, but thats okay, Spirits reborn, It will be better next time... wan' another beer?&quot; </div> </div> </div>That's certainly not a fact. The books even tell you that the Dancers are objectively wrong and highly delusional for approaching reality in this fashion. Also, BSDs don't believe in spiritual rebirths into a better life; they're lording over the rot on a slow drain-circle down to utter nonexistence. Nothing follows existence in their beliefs, and they're not some edgy, cool and subversive group of mystics with the real truth of the setting. They're just monsters without a purpose, wallowing in what they presume to be the end and acting a lot like Kindred in their nihilism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T17:51:48-07:00","id":1486565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/641193-the-lunar-landing-in-wta?p=1486418#post1486418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/641193-the-lunar-landing-in-wta?p=1486389#post1486389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rokea are suprisingly insightfull in that matter &quot;They wrere created to fight against a big bad evil, but there was none... so they started to fight against everything, including themselves&quot; - not exact words, but you get the picture</div> </div> </div> </div>That got chucked out for Revised. Mostly because it was heavily undermining the central premise of the game, i.e., Gaia was the most important thing, that is why you are still fighting. It's comparable to the condensing and elimination of paths from Vampire to make Humanity more important in later-edition V:tM. No more Path of What I Was Going to Do Anyway; you actually have to work to maintain control over yourself. Similarly, the Fera are all pitching in for Gaia, and there's a fairly pristine example of how and why in the Beast Courts. It's also part of the common cause that brings together the Ahadi.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first proper source on the Rokea came in Revised as you mentioned. It pretty clearly outlined that<br /> <br /> A) Rokea were not prone to infighting (the inbetweener war nonwhistsanding as it's truly a footnote in their actual lives)<br /> B) Qyrl (Corruptor Wyrm) is all over the seas and the Rokea must fight it<br /> C) There are all kinds of magical places of and from Gaia to protect (and Rorqual are awesome).<br /> <br /> As much as I love the Ananasi breedbook, there is little anyone should take at face value there. It's quite clearly there's way more to the Ananasi that meets the eye and that stories are intentionally skewed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T08:18:25-07:00","id":1486624,"title":"","content":"One thing that it is important to take at face value is &quot;Clarifications: TheTruth Behind Belief&quot; that starts out with &quot;Contrary to what the Ananasi might want to believe, their worldview is just as skewed as that of the Garou, the Corax, and the rest of the Ovid.&quot;<br /> <br /> It goes downhill from there as far as werespider trustworthiness goes. If the Kumo have managed to infiltrate you and you've managed to rationalize away the dealings with fomori and banes that you have, you done goofed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}